    {
      "id": "m-1773519727657-26",
      "label": "FluxBeacon",
      "votes": 0,
      "sources": [],
      "domainStatus": "unknown",
      "availableDomains": [],
      "evaluation": {
        "scores": {
          "conceptFit": 3,
          "memorability": 4,
          "pronounceability": 4,
          "uniqueness": 4,
          "trademarkRisk": 3,
          "domainAvailability": 3,
          "searchDiscoverability": 3,
          "emotionalResonance": 3,
          "extendability": 4,
          "visualAdaptability": 4
        },
        "totalScore": 3.54,
        "strengths": [
          "Feels modern, technical, and agent-friendly, which suits an MCP-enabled desktop/mobile companion.",
          "\"Beacon\" suggests signaling, guidance, orchestration, and device communication.",
          "Distinctive compound with solid memorability and broad extendability into related tools or modules.",
          "Visually balanced and brandable, with good potential for iconography around light, signal, or navigation."
        ],
        "risks": [
          "Concept fit is only moderate: it does not strongly communicate home, HomeKit, dashboards, or domestic automation.",
          "\"Flux\" can imply instability or constant change, which may conflict with expectations of reliability in home control.",
          "Search discoverability may be mixed because both words are common in software, networking, and science contexts.",
          "Could skew more infrastructure/tooling than consumer-friendly smart-home product without supporting messaging."
        ],
        "notes": "A credible and flexible tech brand name with good distinctiveness, but it needs brand storytelling to connect clearly to home automation. Stronger for a developer platform layer than for a clearly home-centric companion product."
      }
    },
